-- ui/DungeonLoot.lua
-- Which bosses in this dungeon can still drop something you would wear.
--
-- GENERATED BY tools/genloot.js - DO NOT EDIT BY HAND.
-- Re-run it after AtlasLoot updates; hand edits are lost on the next run.
--
-- The ids are HARVESTED from AtlasLoot's Ascension build, never authored. Writing item
-- ids from memory would produce confident nonsense - an addon that tells you to leave a
-- dungeon your boots were in - and there is no way to check one from outside the game.
--
-- `bosses` are killable encounters (AtlasLoot marks them with BabbleBoss). `extra` is
-- everything else it lists - trash tables, quest items, vendor sections. Extras count as
-- a reason to STAY but are never expected to die, so they cannot sit in the remaining
-- list forever and stop the prompt from ever firing.
--
-- ============================================================================
-- THE RULE THIS DATA IS SHAPED AROUND
-- ============================================================================
--   A dungeon that is not listed produces NO ADVICE AT ALL. Not "nothing here for you" -
--   silence. The absence of data must never read as the presence of a negative answer.
--
--   A boss with an empty item list is treated as UNKNOWN, not as empty. Same reason.
--
-- Ascension is a modified server, and AtlasLoot can be wrong or behind. /valuate dungeon
-- says exactly what is known for where you are standing, so a wrong entry is visible
-- rather than silently steering you.
--
-- 36 dungeons, 264 bosses, 2918 items.

